WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.880
Depression is a complex disease, one
that can be triggered by several factors,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.860
including chemical imbalances in the
brain, medical conditions, traumatic

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.220
life events, and genetics. But depression
can start to lift within just a

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.720
few weeks, provided you find the right
combination of effective treatments.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.100
This is Your Brain On, where we explore
how the world affects our brains

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.120
and ourselves. Brain imaging studies
show that depression is connected to

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.820
changes in several parts of the
brain, especially in three core areas.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.920
The first is the amygdala, which
regulates emotions like anger, pleasure,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.040
and fear. When a person is depressed,
the amygdala can become overactive,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.020
causing problems with sleep and
behavior, as well as balance of key mood

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.540
hormones. The second area is the
hippocampus, which processes memory and

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.440
regulates stress hormones
such as cortisol.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.580
One study found it's up to 13% smaller
in depressed women, and excess cortisol

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.840
can stunt the growth of new neurons,
creating poor moods and memory.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.220
The third main area is the thalamus,
which helps link sensory information

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.300
to good and bad feelings. Problems in
the thalamus may be linked to conditions

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.320
such as bipolar disorder. Changes to
these parts of the brain and others

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.160
mess with key hormones such as serotonin,
which regulates sleep and mood,

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.820
and norepinephrine,
which affects motivation.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.620
For some, a depressed mood passes on
its own, especially if it was triggered

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.340
by a particular sad event. But for
those with ongoing clinical depression,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.660
it can take time to find
effective treatment.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.400
Stats show sticking with
treatment is worth it.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.400
One study by the National Institutes
of Health showed 80% of people improved

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.240
within just four to six weeks of
starting medication, therapy, or support

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.020
groups. Healthy lifestyle
choices can help, too.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.680
Eating a good diet and getting enough
sleep can strengthen and repair important

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.740
brain connections. Overcoming depression
may become easier in the future.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.460
Scientists are learning more about
how factors such as genetics influence

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.740
depression, which may not only help
create new drugs, but also make targeted

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.780
treatment possible, helping someone
with depression feel like herself again.
